ioned numbers  are one of the most vital details in  zelda lore you have the three pieces of  the triforce  four giants in majora's mask five adult  dungeons in ocarina of time  six elements of the universe and seven  total sages including the leader  zelda herself these numbers are all  specific and not debatable when birth  the wild first released  fans were amazed at the sheer amount of  shoutouts and easter eggs placed around  the world of hyrule that were all  somehow referencing the games of the  past stumbling across these seven heroin  statues in the desert  led the vast majority of fans to come to  the conclusion that the number was meant  to represent the sages from ocarina of  time  since that's the only other time the  number 7 appears in zelda law  however there are some issues with this  assumption that i would like to point  out firstly and most obviously there are  actually 8 of them even though the  heroin  shrine that appears when you match their  symbols with their corresponding orbs  only needs seven orbs to be matched  implying initially that the eight might  not matter the fact instead is that  there are quests associated with the  eight  and there is indeed an eight giant  heroin statue on the far  side of mount the gods which is simply  too large of a detail to  ignore secondly if the seven sages are  to be represented by seven heroines  that must mean that one of them has to  represent the leader  princess zelda herself as she is the  only reason there are seven  sages in the first place however none of  these statues feature any unique  characteristics that might  serve to distinguish the leader from the  others except for this one which sword  has broken but that's probably nothing  you would think that the actual tangible  physical incarnation of goddess hylia  who also happens to be the princess of  legend as well as leader of the sages  would merit some sort of distinction  amongst the group  lastly the heroines are located in the  gerudo desert  this might be a small detail but if you  think about it that is a strange  location to represent the sages of  hyrule  the masters or chamber in the wind waker  is the only area in the game  paying tribute to the sages from ocarina  of time and it's located in hyrule  castle  the home of the hylian royal family who  protect the triforce which is what this  entire franchise is really about  placing a tribute to the seven sages who  apparently are actually  eight without any distinction or  representation of the legion  here in the gerudo desert of all places  is why we feel there is another  explanation for the status mysteries  very well said sir it's clear that using  the seven  sages of yore to explain the eight  statues isn't the most  neatly fitting option so let's talk  about what might be  instead what if the eight statues don't  represent the sages  but rather the eight races of hyrule  wait are there really eight races in the  land of hyrule  there are you have the hylians the chica  the gorons the rito  the zora the gerudo the forest dwellers  also known as koroks also known as  kokori and the allegedly extinct ancient  barbarian race known as  the zonai that's right this video is  also kind of a zonai theory  if you came here from commonwealth  realms video though i guess you already  knew that  but back to the races of hyrule as you  can see there are seven statues with one  removed from the others  and in hyrule there are seven races of  hyruleans with one removed from the  others interesting isn't it  but the proof for this is more than just  numbers and somewhat vague similarities  you see even though we previously stated  that these statues don't possess  any unique identifying traits that was  only somewhat true  there are actually two very unique  identifying traits that all of the  statues share  the first being their oddly specific  powers that they're each said to  represent  skill spirit endurance knowledge flight  motion and gentleness the second unique  trait being the unique symbols that they  each have somewhere on their surface  except for the removed statue the eighth  these seven symbols are used in a kind  of matching game with corresponding orbs  to make a shrine appear but what if they  were more than just  random symbols i mean nintendo is very  specific when it comes to symbology in  zelda games  they've used symbols since the original  games to represent ideas  artifacts or even people groups i think  it's fair to assume that the seven  symbols represent the seven  powers spoken of by the gerudo legend  but let's take that  one step further and try to test this  racial symbology by matching the powers  and corresponding symbols to the  hyrulean races  actually i've already matched the powers  and races together and i'm just going to  skip explaining all of that for the sake  of time  let's start with what is far and away  the most compelling and obvious piece of  evidence for  all of this symbology the gentleness  symbol or in my opinion  the symbol of the koroks you see this  symbol is actually an  exact representation of the classic  kokiri symbol seen in ocarina of time  and as mentioned before  the modern day koroks and ancient kokori  are actually the same race of forest  dwellers  not only is it already very similar in  shape to the symbols seen on the kokori  shield but  if you add in the emerald portion to the  kokori emblem  it literally becomes the same symbol the  others are admittedly not quite as  obvious as this one but with the  specific attention to detail that the  zelda developers have for symbology in  this very game  the forest dweller gentleness symbol  seems to be undeniable  the other symbols are a bit more  debatable as they're all unique to this  game  but we'll try to place them with the  most likely options  the gorons represented by endurance are  most likely the symbol here that  resembles an  upward pointed arrow this could be a  reference to a mountain or more  specifically death mountain which the  corons famously  live on the sheikah represented by  knowledge are most likely this symbol  which resembles an open  eye similar to the other more well-known  symbol the rito represented by flight  are most likely the symbol which  resembles a sleeker upward arrow  referencing to the sky the zora  represented by motion  are most likely this symbol that  resembles a wave or stream of water the  gerudo represented by skill  are most likely this simple here that is  just two dots  one on top of the other this is one of  the more vague symbols but we have  decided it's most likely the gerudo due  to the process of elimination  and the use of evenly spaced dots which  are at least somewhat similar to the  other more well-known  symbol finally the hylians represented  by spirit  are most likely this symbol that closely  resembles a real-life  horse site this is of course due to the  process of elimination but could also be  a representation of the equal  or even statues that hylians share with  all the other races of hyrule  they are like the glue that holds them  all together the symbols may all be  unique to these statues  since they were created by the ancient  gerudo who probably came up with their  own symbols to represent the other races  why they got the forest dweller symbol  down accurately however is yet to be  determined  then there is the matter of the eighth  statue the forgotten one  that has no representation of power or  symbol  while the zone i famously have a swirl  as their alleged symbol  this isn't necessarily proven to be  accurate in the game and the fact that  they have no symbols or powers  associated with the statue  is actually in line with the status of  being forgotten or we know  they could have gone extinct before even  the statues were created  as with many things in breath of the  wild this is still pretty vague stuff  but given all the similarities and  evidence and symbology we just talked  about  this seems to be the most likely  solution to the age-old mystery of the  heroin statues but what do you guys  think  are they the gerudos ancient  representations of the eight races of  hyrule  or somehow still representations of the  sages or something else entirely let me  know in the comments below  also huge thanks to conrad from the  commonwealth realm for helping out with  this theory and being the person behind  the idea in the first place  and huge thanks to you for watching if  you enjoyed it please consider dropping  a like below to get this spread around  on youtube as that is literally how it  works on this platform and subscribe if  you haven't already to stick around for  more theories and nintendo content just  like this  also humongous thanks to my supporters  who make my day  every day say hello to claire e  melmellow  and connor h who have all joined my  elite bandit crew  if you're interested in doing the same  and helping make the next video come to  life and also maybe help put some food  on my table  click that join button located below or  follow the links in the description to  my patreon page  also down there are the links to my  social media pages so come on over and  say hi on twitter  it's free oh also happy valentine's day  at some point today do yourself a favor  and check out my valentine's day special  where i read your zelda pickup lines  it's it's something alright anyway  that's all i've got  this is masentana bennett signing out  have a great rest of your day  peace  [Music]
 

